===Etymology 2===
{{ety|en|:bor|pt:lancha|:influence|launch<id:throw>|id=boat}}
From {{der|en|pt|lancha||barge, launch}}, apparently from {{der|en|ms|lancar||quick, agile}}. Spelling influenced by the verb above.<ref>{{R:Online_Etymology_Dictionary}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[boat]] of the largest size and/or of most importance belonging to a [[ship]] of war, and often called the "captain's boat" or "captain's launch".
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A boat used to convey guests to and from a [[yacht]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} An open boat of any size powered by steam, [[petrol]], electricity, etc.

